                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]A big open world, completely devoid of content and features...[/h1]\nI completely appreciate the fact that this game comes from a solo developer, but there's just so much missing from the game that I can't recommend it, even at just $6.\n\nCons: #1. No skill tree, passives, talents, or experience gain. There's literally no character progression at all.\n#2. The game is a vast void of nothingness. I spent 2 minutes running from one place to another, and there was NOTHING to interact with during those 2 minutes of running. No loot, no enemies, nothing. What's the point of making a huge open world, if it's devoid of content?\n#3. I played as the Mage class. You can only cast 1 spell (fireball), and you can only cast it when you are full mana, which means when you cast your fireball, you have to wait around 8seconds to cast another. So, the entire mage class is: Fireball, wait 8sec, fireball, wait 8sec, fireball, wait 8sec, fireball, wait 8sec...\n#4. The game has no weapons and no armor, or rings, or nothing (no gear whatsoever).\n#5. Picking up items from the ground is like trying to shoot a fly with a BB-gun. The 'interaction hitbox' of many items is so tiny that you spend 15seconds just trying to pick up a single item.\n#6. The controls / keybindings aren't shown ANYWHERE in the game. It's not even shown in the options menu, so you have to press every key on the keyboard just to figure out what keys actually do something in the game. Spoilers: J-Journal, I-Inventory, C-Character, M-Map, P-Pause, F-Fireball, H-Heal, Space-Jump, Shift-Sprint.\n#7. Many of the controls (like those mentioned above) can't be rebound or customized.\n#8. No health bars, or information on enemies whatsoever. You are given NO information about enemies. Some enemie types take 2hits to kill, and other enemie types take 30hits to kill.... which is which? Nobody knows.\n#9. No saving and no loading slots. The game seemingly does persistent saving (but I can't be sure), so there's no do-overs at all.\n\nI'll keep the game in my library instead of refunding it and check back on the game in a couple of years, but man-oh-man.... I was expecting way way more content and playability from a game that's been in development for 9years already. Best of luck to you dev.\n\nFor more reviews, visit my curator page: https://store.steampowered.com/curator/7851637/\nFor my full recommended list of games: https://steamcommunity.com/id/lfpg/recommended/",
